: Hello everybody,

:    I have a XP1000 workstation with true64 4.0F. Recently it shuts
: down after a couple of hours with the message:

: bs_osf_complete: metadata write failed
: AdvFS Domain Panic; Domain usr_domain Id 0x3819....
: An AdvFS domain panic has occurred due to either a metadata write
: error or an internal inconsistency. This domain is being rendered
: inaccesible.
: ....

: This has hapened a lot of times during the last month and I am
: wondering what is the cause of it and how to fix it. I haven't
: installed any patches yet.
: I would appreciate any help you could give me.

The disk that contains "usr_domain" may be having bad blocks or other errors.
To look at the error log, use:

        # uerf -Rr 199 -o full | more
        
Which will look at CAM errors (record type 199), in reverse order (most recent
first) and give a full output.  If you don't know how to read the error log
data that it gives you, post a couple of entries.

