> changes that forced source level recompiles? 

The SunOS->Solaris was pretty bad in many respects. Some old user-mode 
executables refused to run, others had abominable performance. And that
was a transition on the same hardware.

IBM's OS/390 upgrades are, AFAIK, all about compatibility at the binary
level. When you recompile to the new models, you will uncover a lot of
the dirty programming tricks that were used. But then, what is new?

