are very few applications that exist on VMS only. So, if application X exists
on Unix with more up-to-date versions and solid commitments whereas on VMS,
you have to fight to get any word from the vendor about their support of VMS,
new customers will continue to ignore VMS and go for platforms whose future
does not include constant fears of vendors dropping support.

