In article <2f6bec0a.0108290000.47fee096@posting.google.com> banny52@yahoo.com (Ginny E. Kim) writes:
>I got a following console message while loading my dynamic kernel
>module
>---------
>load failed: no configuration entrypoint
>----------
>what's the problem?

That last line: "no configuration entrypoint" is the problem.

A loadable module "xyz.mod" must have an entry point xyz_configure()
that is called to configure and start the module. There must also be
an attributes table xyz_attributes[] with any tunable parameters in it.
The table can be empty, the configure routine must at least be able to
return 0.

