> ...)(0))->pcb)&127)?-1:1" can't be positive interger?

Ginny:
	This is a poor-man's way to ensure that the pcb member of
   	the stack_layout structure is properly aligned.  In your
	compilation, the pcb member was not aligned properly so
	the the size of the _pcb_align_check array was -1, which
 	intentionally results in a compile-time error.  
	(Note that since this was added, the compiler has added 
	pragmas to support this kind of compile-time checking.)

	It looks like you are either building your module wrong or
	you've modified something that caused the size/layout of
	the stack_layout struct to change.
Joe

