The critical part is restoring the boot disks and the cluster common
disks.  These should be backed up using vdump.  The application
executables and data should be backed up using Legato NETworker or
equivalent Enterprise wide backup application.  If they are to restore
from Legato NETworker, then the /nsr disk should be backed up with vdump
also.  This allows restoration of all the critical pieces prior to
recreating the storage configuration.  A sys_check should be run on the
system, then move the html file off-system to a pc or other location.
This will give enough detail to recreate the storage configuration, LSM
volumes, AdvFS file systems, environmental variables, etc. for the
Disaster Recovery process.



