And that's something that both TOPS-10 and TOPS-20 were pretty good at
given sufficient memory. When I first ran some tests of a 2060 and a
VAX 11/780 side by side I put the 2060 around five times the speed of
the 780 at running compiled code. However if you took a
compile/link/debug cycle you were more like ten to one or worse. I
recall a LISP interpreter written in Pascal compiled on the 2060 in 10
seconds (Chuck Hedrick's SPascal) but took around 300 secs to compile
under DEC Pascal. As Pascal was one of the main teaching languages we
used at the time this caused considerable problems. even with DEC
compilers on both TOPS-20 and VMS a typical Fortran compilation took
around 10 times as long as on a 780 as on a 2060.

