Compilation on VMS typically took a long time in the early days and
you seemed more likely to hit IO/bandwidth/RMS bottlenecks (which
could sometimes be 'fixed' by tuning which was nowhere near as
important on TOPS-20). Over the years improvements to VMS and the
enormous increase in processor power (I consider the 780 to have been
way underpowered from day 1 and telling TOPS-10/20 shops that this was
the future drove huge numbers away. I still know IT managers who won't
talk to DEC/Compaq on principle because of this). And now Compaq have
just announced the murder of another architecture.

