>How can I use 'monitor replay' to play back the data faster than I
>recorded it?  For example, if I sample data every five minutes for an
>hour, I have not been able to figure out how to play back my
>monitor.dat file in less than an hour.

The -sleep options sets the sampling interval for both live data
collection and replay from a file.  So:

% monitor replay -sleep 2

Pressing a key will also trigger getting a new sample.  This works
fine for small files where you want time to interpret the data.  I
typically use the space bar.

