Hello,

In your post I do not see the add unit command.  The process is:

Add Disk

or

run config (this command will poll the hsg80 for available devices

then:

Add Raid r9 disk10000 disk20000 disk 30000 and so on

then:

Add Unit d# r9

This will send the raidset off for a couple of hours depending on the size.
You should see the lights flickering on the devices that makeup the raidset.
You will get back to the hsg80 prompt so if you have a number of raidsets
that you will create units for, you can initalize multiple raidsets.  A 5
member R5 set comprised of 18 G drives will take around 2 -or 3 hours.

Remember T64 will only see the unit identifier.

BTW, I am assuming that you are running T64 V5.1

You may also want to add a uuid to the unit so that from T64 you will be
able to identify your new device by running the command

#hwmgr -show devices (refer to man pages for more options)

Adding a Disk to 5.1 Cluster:

Run this on each member
hwmgr -scan comp -cat scsi_bus

Wait a minute for all the members to register the new disk then:

/usr/sbin/clu_disk_install

To learn the name of the new disk you can run:

#hwmgr -view devices -cluster

If you are running 4.0X with 1.6 clustering, sorry you are on your own...

Regards
Peter Barone
Compaq Services



