Compaq is pleased to announce the field test of our latest Developers'
Toolkit Supplement for Tru64 UNIX. The field test is free and open to all
developers. The kit can be downloaded from:

http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/dtk/

This new version of the DTK Supplement will install and run on Tru64 UNIX
versions V4.0F, V4.0G, V5.0A, V5.1and V5.1A and contains new-and-improved
versions of the following development tools:

Compaq C-a standards-compliant, full-featured, highly optimizing compiler
specifically developed to exploit the 64-bit Alpha architecture

Spike-a post-link optimizer that is particularly effective when utilizing
application profile information

Visual Threads-a debugging and analysis tool for multi-threaded applications
that helps users detect deadlock, thread usage errors,shared data protection
problems, and poor performance

Ladebug-a powerful, multi-language, source-level debugger

Program Analysis Tools - a suite of debugging and profiling tools that
includes third (for detecting memory problems), hiprof (for call graph
profiling), pixie (for

profile directed optimization and test coverage analysis), and atom (a
binary instrumentation toolkit for writing new tools).

Graphical Program Analysis Tools-a graphical user interface for the program
analysis tools, a heap profiler, and a process monitor.

The field test is expected to last until the official product is released in
October. Field test customers are invited to send feedback via the website.





