Michiel Roos wrote:
> 
> >
> > Tru64  (I think it's called AlphaBIOS,ARC or SRM)
> 
>  The difference between ARC and SRM is for booting different operating
> systems. With one (I think it was SRM) you can boot Windows NT, the
> other firmware will only load Tru64. Not sure which is which.
> 

 It is the other way round. You have SRM and ARC/AlphaBIOS.

 - AlphaBIOS boots NT and Linux (using MILO).
 - SRM boots Tru64, VMS, Linux (using aboot), and probably any other OS
as long as the disk is BSD-labelled and there is a working bootloader at
block 0 (or wherever it belongs :-). SRM is actually pretty similar to
the SGI PROM Monitor.

Martin
