The Arc/Alphabios firmware is a GUI type firmware used for booting NT
and can also be used for booting some free unix-alikes (I can't remember
if it was Linux or FreeBSD I booted this way).
The SRM firmware is a command line based firmware which will run on a
graphics head or a serial console and is used for booting Tru64 and OpenVMS.

Hope this helps
Adam





