In article <1dc0fc17.0108160043.2192c2da@posting.google.com>, gerold@mail.com (Gerold Schweikart) writes:
>
>Situation:
>Want to backup on AlphaServer, Tru64 Unix 4.0F which has Tape Loader
>TL891 and Media Robot Utility.
>Backup is done with cpio commands within brbackup of SAP R/3 4.6c
>
>Problem:
>Most of the backups need one tape, ROBOT commands work fine.
>
>One of the backups requires two tapes:
>First tape gets full, second tape is autoloaded. Then Robot Utility
>command "robot unload ..." brings error message "robot not ready".

The TL891 operates in one of two modes; sequential loading and random
access.  In sequential loading a SCSI Unload command sent to the drive
will cause the media changer to load the tape from the magazine.  Use
of this feature completely disables the ability to use the media
changer for random access.  When set for random access mode, the
media changer accepts SCSI-2 Media Changer commands (such as sent
by MRU) allowing any tape to be loaded from the magazine.

When I learned that the TL891 was going behave this way, I told the
relevant engineering it was a poor idea, but they didn't want my
advice.  My recollection is that "robot not ready" is the condition
that occurs when the library is in sequential loading mode.  But,
it has been a couple of years since I looked.

