Hi all,
I got the information I was looking for and deemed it appropriate to share
it with the group.

There is a problem with sprintf , printf, vsprintf etc. when you use
RWCString or SString.

For example if you do:

RWCString s("Hello World");
char buf[32];
sprintf(buf,"%s",s);

You get a  Seg Fault!

You should therefore use:

sprintf(buf,"%s",(const char *)s);

With warm regards,
-Venkatesh Prasad R.


