Zoong Pham <dpham@mercy.com.au> wrote:
> in our cluster (V5.1), the caad daemon died unexpectedly.
> I couldn't find the reason why it died.
> Any hint ?

In our cluster (2xES40, 5.0A) the caad died several times.

It seems that "bouncing" cluster apps kill the daemon after
a time: part of cluster app fails, caad tries to restart it,
restart times out, cluster app goes down, caad tries to
restart it, etc. Until caad dies on the member with the
"bouncing" app.

Wolfgang Rupp



