Florian Weps <fweps@pop.agri.ch> wrote in message news:<m2ofpjegob.fsf@localhost.localdomain.localnet>...

> I *think* the reason for 4.0G's existence is that Q wanted to cater to
> customers who weren't ready to move to 5.x, yet still wanted to buy a
> Wildfire. Thus, it is a 4.0x with support for Wildfire. I could be
> wrong.

That is correct, for loose definitions of the word "support".  

Techincally, 4.0g does provide support for Wildfire, but it's best
to keep your partitions down to a single QBB.  4.0g is not NUMA aware,
ie it has no knowledge of QBBs, RADs, or the overhead required for 
access accross the Wildfire's switch, so it generally is a poor performer
on multi-QBB partitions.  It's at best a crutch for shops to limp on
while they migrate to 5.1.

HTH

