news:8iffnt8178nrckh0p20hc18b8u9rg52ntl@4ax.com...
>
> I've scanned in the letter from Compaq and OCRd it. Here is the text
> of the letter. I can email a physical scanned image if anyone needs
> one.
...
> As a result of this retirement, Compaq SOFTWARE Services (ie license
> subscription, software update distribution services and software
> telephone support) will no longer be available for the above items as
> of 30th Jan 2002. Note hardware maintenance continues for the above
> items.

What this means is that they're not going to take your money to do software
maintenance; there probably no one doing any software maintenance on those
products, and hasn't been for some time, so that means that they now going
to charge you what the service is worth: zero.

Any problems will end up being VMS's responsibility because they will
basically be caused by a change in the VMS driver for DSSI, CI, or SCSI.
For VAX, those components are probably untouched for some time, other than a
few more bug fixes to further increase the stability.

> A migration path is offered with 50% off the storage controller price
> (le HSG8O and HSJ8Os). We can also offer leasing options for those who
> would prefer to lease the new storage controllers and associated
> equipment.

This statement is in there because this is an opportunity to generate
business.  This is an upgrade so Compaq gets functional modules back which
can be recycled into the spares needed to maintain the existing installed
base and a few upgrades from the customers who bought the gear recently
enough for this to make sense.  For the other customers who check into the
upgrade, it is an opportunity for the sales rep to replace the entire
storage system.

The only problem is that in most areas the storage sales reps don't
understand the environments with these systems, especially VMS, so they are
going to be slow to contact the customer because they have simpler sales to
go after.  If the sales rep does know VMS (the rare old time DEC sales guy),
he's already concluded that there's no upgrade path, otherwise he would have
been selling it already.





