In article <MPG.15d99db58c0131649896eb@news.siol.net>, Marvin
<glodalec@yahoo.com> wrote:

X  I would like to mount NFS partition using timeo=15 option. It can be 
X  done using mount manually, but checking man fstab, there is no such 
X  option. How to make partition mounted at the boot time with timeo option
X  (without making special script in rc.* directory ?)

add any mount -o options to the fstab field 4 'mnt_options'.  The fstab
man page says:

        See mount(8) for a complete list and description of 
        the legal mount options for the various file system 
        types.
So in your case, you would want to specify the fstab entry as:

    node:/dir/to/export  /mnt  nfs  nfsv3,ro,bg,timeo=15  0 0

where ro and bg are just something I threw in to show the comma
separation between mount options.  Use whatever set of NFS mount
options you prefer.

                                        Bob Harris


