>"Error: can't read "dskdir" no such variable."

What partition are you using?  Once the disk is labeled, if you use
the C partition it should use the whole disk.  I tend to use the
disklabel command directly when I want to change the partition
table, but I'm old fashioned that way.

>
>If I try to use mkfdmn /dev/rrz1h disk1, it returns the errors:
>mkfdmn: can't get device size; not a block device
>mkfdmn: can't create new domain disk1

You have to use the block device with the mkfdmn command.  /dev/rrz
is the character device.  /dev/rz is the block device.

