Till recently I was using dump/restore to perform backups using an
autoloader operating in sequential mode. When dump fills up a tape,
the autoloader would eject the tape and load the next one. Dump would
print a message to the terminal requesting that a tape be loaded, but
would poll the tape drive in the autoloader to see if it had a tape
loaded and would continue with the dump if it did. This worked
perfectly for years.

I have started to use AdvFS and as a result have to use
vdump/vrestore. In my tests, vdump behaves differently from dump in
that when vdump fills up a tape, the autoloader will eject the tape
and load the next one and vdump will print a message to the terminal
requesting that the next tape be loaded, but it does not poll the tape
drive in the autoloader to see if it has a tape loaded and will not
continue with the vdump if it does. Instead vdump sits there waiting
for the operator to hit that enter key when the tape is loaded.

This is a pain when I am running backups through cron. If there are no
vdump options to make it work like dump, I will have to use expect,
but I would like to avoid that if possible.

