Misc 11 -- How do I deal with the swap file filling up?
=========================================================================

Remove the file /sbin/swapdefaults and reboot.

Digital UNIX has two paging modes, lazy and conservative.  Conservative
means
that paging space is allocated as memory is allocated, guaranteeing  that
there
is always somewhere to page to.  This limits VM to the  size of the paging
partitions, but makes for a very robust system.  Lazy is more like what
people
are used to with Unix - paging space  is allocated when needed for paging
out,
you can run more jobs, but  you're in big trouble when everything fills up.
By
default, Digital UNIX comes up in the conservative mode.   Removing the
swapdefaults file changes the system to lazy mode.

