This works, provided you are careful.

Something along the lines of:

- install new disks
- RUN CONFIG 
- ADD RAID NEWDATA <disk1> <disk2> <disk3> <disk4> <disk5> <disk6>
- ADD UNIT D2
- newfs mount copy etc
- DELETE UNIT D2
- DELETE UNIT D1 (old unit)
- remove 18 Gigs
- DELETE DATA1 # don;t worry
- DELETE NEWDATA #    ditto
- move disks ***in the right order***  to new location
- ADD RAID  DATA1 <disk1-in-new-position> <...> etc
- ADD UNIT D1 DATA1

I would always make a backup btw ;)

