In article <3b680f61$0$7117$4d4efb8e@news.be.uu.net>, MIKA
<mika@robot.cvo> wrote:

X  Thanks Bob for your explication
X  but sorry may be for this stupid question
X  What is Mcell mean ?

Metadata Cell.  Metadata is the term we use to describe all the
information the file system needs to keep about a file so that it can
keep track of where the file is on the disk, its size, data
information, etc...  Metadata is also the other file system information
such as the storage bitmap used to find free space, metadata to
maintain the domain information, metadata to maintain the individual
fileset information, metadata to maintain the frag file inforamtion,
etc...

In the UFS world the closest analog to the Mcell would be the inode,
except that in UFS a file gets only 1 inode, but the UFS inode may have
any number of indirect pages for mapping the storage of larger files. 
In AdvFS the Mcell is a generic bucket where some Mcells are the
primary Mcell holding most of the same kind of information as a UFS
inode, or additional Mcells may be chained to the primary Mcell to
contain additional file information, such as storage extent maps,
property lists, clone information, etc...

Mcells do _NOT_ contain all the metadata for the file system, just
information related to individual files.
  
