X> storage is allocated and attached to the clone's Mcell, then the
pages
X> about to be modified are copied to the newly allocated clone storage.
X>
X> Any additional modifications to the same pages, will _NOT_ be copied
to
X> the clone, since it is only the first modifications to any given page
X> that are copied to the clone.
X>
X> If the file is deleted or truncated, then all the deleted pages are
X> given to the clone Mcell.
X>
X> If a file is renamed, this is actually a modification to a directory,
X> and the directory pages are copied to its clone Mcell.
X>
X> Creating new files only affects the clone in that, creating file is a
X> directory modification.
X>
X> The domain should show less free space over time as modifications to
X> previously untouched pages are made.
X>
X> The way to see the clone is to mount the cloned fileset.  This will
X> present an image of the fileset at the time the clone was snapped. 
If
X> a file was not changed, then the original file will be displayed.  If
X> only some of a file's pages were changed, then the unchanged pages
will
X> come from the original file, and the modified pages will come from
the
